# Which host machines may START sessions on this team's relay.
#
# One public key per line, OpenSSH authorized_keys format: the "relay
# login key" that pairing-setup's installer prints on each host, e.g.
#   ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA... relay login key (pairing@jans-mac)
#
# Empty means nobody can host: the relay starts closed. Add hosts via a
# pull request; whoever runs the relay then applies the list with
#   ./deploy.sh <relay-host> --hosts-only
# (that restarts the relay, which drops sessions in progress).
